```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Sola Stopwatch</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .stopwatch {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 2em;
            color: #333;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="stopwatch" id="stopwatch">00:00:00</div>
    <button onclick="startStopwatch()">Start</button>
    <button onclick="pauseStopwatch()">Pause</button>
    <button onclick="resetStopwatch()">Reset</button>

    <script>
        let startTime;
        let elapsedTime = 0;

        function startStopwatch() {
            if (!startTime) {
                startTime = Date.now();
                updateTimer();
            }
        }

        function pauseStopwatch() {
            if (startTime) {
                clearInterval(interval);
                startTime = null;
            }
        }

        function resetStopwatch() {
            clearInterval(interval);
            elapsedTime = 0;
            document.getElementById('stopwatch').textContent = '00:00:00';
            startTime = null;
        }

        function updateTimer() {
            const now = Date.now();
            const elapsed = now - startTime;
            const minutes = Math.floor(elapsed / (1000 * 60));
            const seconds = Math.floor((elapsed % (1000 * 60)) / 1000);
            const milliseconds = Math.floor((elapsed % 1000) / 10);

            document.getElementById('stopwatch').textContent = `${minutes.toString().padStart(2, '0')}:${seconds.toString().padStart(2, '0')}:${milliseconds.toString().padStart(2, '0')}`;

            interval = setInterval(updateTimer, 10);
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Structure**:
   - A `div` element with the class `stopwatch` to display the elapsed time.
   - Three buttons: "Start", "Pause", and "Reset".

2. **CSS Styling**:
   - Basic styling for the stopwatch and buttons.

3. **JavaScript Logic**:
   - `startTime`: Tracks when the stopwatch starts.
   - `elapsedTime`: Keeps track of the total elapsed time in milliseconds.
   - `updateTimer` function updates the stopwatch every 10 milliseconds, calculating the current time since `startTime`, converting it to minutes, seconds, and milliseconds, and updating the display.
   - `startStopwatch`: Starts the timer if not already running.
   - `pauseStopwatch`: Stops the timer if running.
   - `resetStopwatch`: Resets the stopwatch to zero and stops the timer.

This code provides a simple yet functional stopwatch component with start, pause, and reset functionalities.

